// Power-off alarm bridge (orphan-audit fix 2026-09-07).
//
// The stock vendor already ships everything below the framework: the AIDL
// vendor.qti.hardware.alarm.IAlarm/default HAL (programs the PMIC RTC alarm) and
// /vendor/bin/power_off_alarm (charger-mode watcher that reboots when the alarm
// hits). What was missing is the system-side client Qualcomm ships as the
// proprietary PowerOffAlarm.apk. This is a from-source re-implementation of that
// tiny app: it speaks the same broadcast protocol DeskClock already uses
// (org.codeaurora.poweroffalarm.action.SET_ALARM / CANCEL_ALARM, extra "time"),
// keeps the same package name so the existing seapp_contexts line
// (com.qualcomm.qti.poweroffalarm -> vendor_qti_poweroffalarm_app, seinfo=platform)
// and DeskClock's setPackage() target both apply, and re-declares the permission
// DeskClock requests (org.codeaurora.permission.POWER_OFF_ALARM).
//
// The AIDL under aidl/ is hand-written from the HAL's ABI: method order is the
// transaction order (cancelAlarm=1, getAlarm=2, getRtcTime=3, setAlarm=4), so it
// must stay alphabetical exactly as declared. Unstable local AIDL is fine here:
// the generated proxy never checks the interface hash.
android_app {
    name: "PowerOffAlarm",
    srcs: [
        "src/**/*.java",
        "aidl/**/*.aidl",
    ],
    aidl: {
        local_include_dirs: ["aidl"],
    },
    resource_dirs: ["res"],
    manifest: "AndroidManifest.xml",
    platform_apis: true,
    certificate: "platform",
    system_ext_specific: true,
    optimize: { enabled: false },
    dex_preopt: { enabled: false },
}
